{
  "comment": "The embed-profile contract — the ONE rule that decides which embedding index is read, how wide its vectors are, and whether the process can use a provider at all. The owner is the Rust crate (`crates/memphis-embed/src/profile.rs`); the TypeScript arm is a projection of it (`src/infra/storage/embed-profile.generated.ts`). Both arms check themselves against THIS file: the Rust runner is `crates/memphis-operator/tests/embed_profile_contract.rs`, the TypeScript runner is `tests/unit/embed-profile-contract.test.ts`. WHY: the rule had four owners and four answers. Measured 2026-11-23 on the operator's host, the service answered `mode: semantic` with dim 1024 while a shell, the CLI and any spawned script answered dim 32 — `DEFAULT_EMBEDDING_DIM`, the width of the LOCAL DETERMINISTIC embedder, applied even with a provider configured — and the index on disk holds 768. WHAT: `dimensionSource` is `env`, `index` or `local-deterministic`; `verdict` is `ok`, `no-provider`, `no-index` or `dimension-mismatch`; `indexPath` is ROOT-RELATIVE so the artefact is the same on every machine. The corpus is fixed on purpose: every case names its own committed fixture index, because a case that read the operator's `~/.memphis/embed/index-v1.json` would answer differently on a fresh machine than on this one.",
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "generatedBy": "scripts/sync-embed-profile-contract.mts",
  "owner": "crates/memphis-embed/src/profile.rs",
  "manifest": {
    "schemaVersion": 1,
